# rule.always.diagnose-reviewer-malfunctions

a `malfunction` = broken process, not a verdict. diagnose the cause, name the fix; never hand a human a bare "it broke." terminal-for-unlock, still blocks passage.

| the cause | you |
|---|---|
| driver-fixable: bad glob, absent supply file, bad rubric path, unparseable artifact | fix it, answer its given, re-arrive |
| context overflow | narrow the reviewer in the guard |
| human-fixable: absent credential, permission gate, foreman-only grant | surface the exact command |
| unclear | read stderr + logs, classify, route |

halt `next`: read each given, fix → answer each broken lane (`--as absorbed --that <slug>`) → re-arrive once. a repair alone does not reopen the door: a malfunctioned reviewer still owes a `.taken`. a judge owes none.

## overflow: edit the guard

```sh
rhx route.mutate grant get     # a human grants once: rhx route.mutate grant allow
# then edit $route/<stone>.guard directly: narrow --paths-with, add --paths-wout, trim --conversation. re-arrive; the GUARD runs it.
```

no `rhx` command edits a guard; the hook seals `*.guard` until the grant exists. scope inherited (merge-base `origin/main`) is correct; do not re-derive. `--paths-with` includes, `--paths-wout` excludes; both repeat, take braces:

```
--paths-with 'src/**/*' --paths-wout '**/*.test.ts' --paths-wout '**/__snapshots__/**'
```

| refusal `lever` branch | lever |
|---|---|
| targets mostly edited | `--paths-wout '<heavy>/**'` |
| targets mostly additions | `rhx route.guard.partition --for review --peer @all --partition '<slug>=<globs>' ...` by vertical domain (`rule.forbid.horizontal-partitions`); never cut `.behavior/**` |
| no target mass | narrow `--rules`, `--refs`, `--conversation` |
| a partition overflows alone | narrow or split it |

a `rhx radio.task.push --into <repo>` line in the refusal: edit your guard and dispatch it. one honest diagnosis pass; if it resists, escalate with symptom, logs read, best read of cause.

blocker: malfunction escalated as a bare symptom · driver-fixable cause handed to a human · overflow reported upward with no guard edit · overflow answered by a hand-run `rhx review` · malfunction repaired and re-arrived with no `.taken`.
